msgid "Disk troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:7
#: c6342834479545f6ab9c64b093e210b4
msgid "\"Out of disk space\" error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:10
#: 74b12d9610874519bf5d7b8178c14483
msgid ""
"If the disk is completely full, you will get an ``Out of disk space`` error "
"that may crash your system because Dom0 does not have enough disk space to "
"work. So it’s good practice to regularly check disk space usage. Running the "
"``df -h`` command in dom0 terminal will show some information, but not "
"include all the relevant details. The Qubes user interface provides "
"a :guilabel:`Qubes Disk Space widget`. If you are unable to access the "
"interface, the command line version is running ``sudo lvs | head`` and "
"looking at top entry for LVM pool. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:21
#: 7ea0d621ac3741658319dc71727d0bd4
msgid ""
"If you run ``df -h``, it only shows the information in the ``root`` line "
"(which is already included in the ``pool00`` line). As you can see, the "
"``sudo lvs | head`` command includes additional important columns ``Data%`` "
"and ``Meta%``, shown in the above example to have the values 89% and 69% "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:23
#: a8e36860648a42e1b0e9a4e3f707db33
msgid ""
"If your system is able to boot, but cannot load a desktop environment, it is "
"possible to login to dom0 terminal with Alt + Ctrl + F2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:25
#: a114488b70434607a97fcac64953ae77
msgid ""
"If this does not work, check the size of ``/var/lib/qubes/qubes.xml``. If it "
"is zero, you’ll need to use one of the file backup (stored in ``/var/lib/"
"qubes/backup``), hopefully you have the current data there. Find the most "
"recent one and place in ``/var/lib/qubes/qubes.xml`` instead of the empty "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:27
#: c50ed90f861e4a119d3a096aae754dd3
msgid ""
"In any case you’ll need some disk space to start the VM. Check ``df -h`` "
"output if you have some. If not, here are some hints how to free some disk "
"space:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:29
#: 93c65f680b11467c9bee105652c16570
msgid "Clean yum cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:37
#: 8bb0f9c30a9349c0a5134335a16eea28
msgid ""
"Delete ``.img`` files of a less important VM, which can be found in ``/var/"
"lib/qubes/appvms/``. Then, when the system is working again, clean up the "
"rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:44
#: d41724f9a74a421fb6bc5309f0ab0042
msgid ""
"With this method, you lose the data of one VM, but it’ll work more reliably."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:46
#: 274edc66cf214e9bb2c827a99c64a598
msgid "Decrease the filesystem safety margin (5% by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/disk-troubleshooting.rst:54
#: ff9c9eca53ec4a1f9eb9bc6276fb7214
msgid ""
"Remove some unneeded files in dom0 home (if you have any, most likely not). "
"Also look for unneeded files in ``/var/log`` in dom0, and ``/var/log/qubes``."
msgstr ""

